I wanted to know if anyone has heard of this trick, and if so, checked
the code to see if it would work. I tried it in Debug mode, and it worked quite
well there, but it seems that Wishing works differently in Debug anyway.

The trick...
(possible spoiler)

get a wand of wishing. 
wish for 3 blessed scrolls of charging
read a blessed scroll of charging, charge WoW
wish for a blessed magic lamp
wish for something with magic lamp... (blessed always gives happy genie)
recharge magic lamp
use magic lamp to wish for WoW

This would seem to give infinite wishes, if it actually works in the
real game... Intuitively, it wouldn't, since wishing for a wand of wishing
gives you a wand with -1 charges... but I've never gotten a WoW outside
of Debug mode...

Is it just because of the obscene nature of Wishing in Debug, or what?



